.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt VIRTIO-NET 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm virtio-net
.Nd virtio network driver and frame service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/virtio-net
.Op Ar bar Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Ar bar_size Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar dma Ns = Ns Ar bytes
.Op Ar irq Ns = Ns Ar line
.Op Ar serve
.Op Ar test
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the userspace driver for a modern (virtio 1.0) PCI network function.  It is
launched by
.Xr devd 8
for a function whose vendor and device ids match the driver table, and it
receives four handles in the documented order: the device BAR (3), the
function's configuration page (4), a DMA buffer (5) and a legacy interrupt (6).
The command-line arguments are the values
.Xr devd 8
appends:
.Va bar ,
.Va bar_size ,
.Va dma
and
.Va irq .
.Pp
The driver resets the function, acknowledges it, negotiates
.Dv VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1
plus the MAC, MTU and link-status features, programs the split RX and TX
virtqueues and then serves the persistent
.Dq nic:
control scheme.  The B39
.Xr raven-proto-net 3
ring lives at a documented offset in the same DMA buffer:
.Bl -tag -width "nic:ring" -compact
.It Pa nic:info
MAC, MTU, link, ring offset/length, descriptor counts, pool length and DMA
length as
.Ql key=value
lines.
.It Pa nic:mac , nic:mtu , nic:link
one line each.
.It Pa nic:ring
attaches the DMA buffer; the consumer maps it and slices
.Ql ring_offset..ring_offset+ring_len .
.It Pa nic:start , nic:stop
arm or pause the frame pump (write one byte).
.It Pa nic:quit
test-only clean shutdown; ignored with
.Er EPERM
otherwise.
.El
.Pp
The ring has 8 RX and 8 TX descriptors and an 11-buffer pool of 2 KiB buffers.
RX pool buffers 0..7 are the device receive buffers; the virtio-net header lands
before the frame, so the RX descriptor points past it.  A TX descriptor names a
pool buffer holding a complete Ethernet frame; the driver submits a
two-descriptor chain (a zero virtio header then the frame) and only advances the
TX consumer index after the device completed the frame.  Every index, length,
buffer offset and frame flag is checked.  Completion is driven by the ISR byte
and the transferred interrupt with a bounded 10 ms wait; a timeout or a malformed
ring resets the device and the driver reports the pump error.
.Pp
A pump thread owns the device so the control scheme stays responsive while
frames flow.  When the driver exits it resets the function; the DMA buffer and
the interrupt line belong to
.Xr devd 8 ,
which closes its own copies after the child exits.
.Pp
Without
.Ar serve
or
.Ar test
the driver keeps the B13b one-shot behaviour (one ARP request and reply, then
exit) for the old
.Ql virtio-net
qtest.  The production driver table uses
.Ar serve ;
the net-b qtest uses
.Ar test .
.Pp
The device must be a modern-only function (for example QEMU's
.Ql virtio-net-pci,disable-legacy=on ) whose registers live in a memory BAR.
Legacy virtio, MSI and MSI-X are not supported yet; the driver uses the
function's legacy INTx line.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/drivers.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/drivers.toml
the driver table that launches
.Nm
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr pcid 8 ,
.Xr raven-proto-net 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
Virtio 1.0 (OASIS), PCI Local Bus 3.0.
